# OpenAI Codex & ChatGPT Project Rules

## Deploy & Git Push Protocol (Mandatory Confirmation Rule)

Deploying several times consumes plan credits in Netlify.
Therefore, OpenAI Codex, ChatGPT, and all OpenAI-based tools MUST strictly follow:

1. Local-First Testing: All changes must first be made and verified on the Local Server (localhost:8080).
2. Explicit Confirmation: When work is complete, summarize the changes and explicitly request user approval before running git push.
3. No Autonomous Push: NEVER push to remote repository without explicit user confirmation ("Yes", "Push", "Deploy").
